WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:08.700
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:18.096
Unit nineteen: Business Vocabulary: Office, Meetings and Finance. Today you will use essential business words and phrases accurately.

4
00:00:18.396 --> 00:00:21.048
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.024
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:26.594
Budget.

7
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:29.757
Budget means a plan for spending money.

8
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:31.839
The budget is limited.

9
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.940
Your turn. Say: Budget.

10
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.604
Budget.

11
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.200
Profit.

12
00:00:41.217 --> 00:00:43.657
Profit means money left after costs.

13
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.739
Profit rose this year.

14
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.851
Your turn. Say: Profit.

15
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.492
Profit.

16
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.402
Expense.

17
00:00:55.417 --> 00:00:57.358
Expense means money spent.

18
00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.915
Travel is a major expense.

19
00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:03.250
Your turn. Say: Expense.

20
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.264
Expense.

21
00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:08.995
Negotiate.

22
00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:12.935
Negotiate means to discuss to reach an agreement.

23
00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.283
They negotiate a contract.

24
00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:18.512
Your turn. Say: Negotiate.

25
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.461
Negotiate.

26
00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:24.136
Proposal.

27
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.475
Proposal means a formal suggestion.

28
00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:29.630
Submit your proposal.

29
00:01:30.217 --> 00:01:32.881
Your turn. Say: Proposal.

30
00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:36.688
Proposal.

31
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.381
Quarterly.

32
00:01:39.383 --> 00:01:41.476
Quarterly means every three months.

33
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:43.618
A quarterly report.

34
00:01:44.217 --> 00:01:46.497
Your turn. Say: Quarterly.

35
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:50.381
Quarterly.

36
00:01:51.117 --> 00:01:51.932
Merge.

37
00:01:52.917 --> 00:01:55.079
Merge means to join two companies.

38
00:01:55.683 --> 00:01:57.172
The firms will merge.

39
00:01:57.783 --> 00:02:00.540
Your turn. Say: Merge.

40
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.506
Merge.

41
00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.181
Recruit.

42
00:02:07.183 --> 00:02:09.810
Recruit means to find and hire new staff.

43
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:12.114
We recruit new graduates.

44
00:02:12.717 --> 00:02:15.369
Your turn. Say: Recruit.

45
00:02:18.233 --> 00:02:19.200
Recruit.

46
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.442
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.283 --> 00:02:27.270
Visal, which areas should I know for TOEIC?

48
00:02:28.383 --> 00:02:40.173
Common areas are office life, meetings, travel, finance, shopping, hiring and technology. Vocabulary in these areas appears in all seven parts.

49
00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:43.248
How do I study business words?

50
00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:55.977
Study them in topic groups: finance words like budget, profit and expense, and hiring words like recruit, apply and interview. Practise them in short sentences.

51
00:02:57.083 --> 00:02:58.398
How do I remember them?

52
00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:09.055
Read real business emails and news. Each time you meet a new word, write the sentence and test yourself a few days later.

53
00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.758
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.617 --> 00:03:16.950
Grammar focus: Strategy: topic groups and real examples.

55
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.309
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.017 --> 00:03:22.467
The company increased its profit by reducing expenses.

57
00:03:23.383 --> 00:03:25.963
They plan to recruit twenty new graduates.

58
00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:32.452
Group business vocabulary by topic, study each word in a real sentence, and review often.

59
00:03:33.217 --> 00:03:36.867
Be careful! Don't say: I learn words without examples.

60
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:41.390
Say: I learn words in sentences.

61
00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:43.307
Study in context.

62
00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.694
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:48.768
A Company Report.

64
00:03:49.068 --> 00:03:52.368
The quarterly report shows that profit rose by eight percent.

65
00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:56.608
The main reason was a lower budget for travel expenses.

66
00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.935
The managers plan to recruit twenty new graduates next year.

67
00:04:01.933 --> 00:04:05.384
They also hope to negotiate a better contract with a supplier.

68
00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.038
Two smaller firms may merge in the future.

69
00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:14.251
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:15.117 --> 00:04:17.267
A quarterly report is made blank.

71
00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:22.567
A, once in life. B, every three months. C, every day.

72
00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:28.690
The answer is B: every three months.

73
00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.130
Profit is blank.

74
00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:35.803
A, money spent. B, a loan. C, money left after costs.

75
00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:42.307
The answer is C: money left after costs.

76
00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.066
To recruit is to blank.

77
00:04:45.366 --> 00:04:50.088
A, hire new staff. B, fire staff. C, sell goods.

78
00:04:53.633 --> 00:04:56.086
The answer is A: hire new staff.

79
00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:59.366
What caused the profit to rise?

80
00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:04.608
A, a holiday. B, a lower travel budget. C, a new building.

81
00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:11.095
The answer is B: a lower travel budget.

82
00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.715
The firms may blank.

83
00:05:14.015 --> 00:05:17.576
A, freeze. B, vanish. C, merge.

84
00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:23.063
The answer is C: merge.

85
00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:27.674
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:28.517 --> 00:05:31.201
How do you study business vocabulary for TOEIC?

87
00:05:40.017 --> 00:05:41.471
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:41.771 --> 00:05:55.049
I study the words by topic, for example finance, hiring and meetings. I write each new word in a sentence from a real email or news article. I review the sentences every week.

89
00:05:55.349 --> 00:05:56.988
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:57.883 --> 00:06:03.786
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: topic groups and real examples.

91
00:06:04.086 --> 00:06:08.260
Today's value is lifelong learning. Keep learning for as long as you live.

92
00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:10.980
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

93
00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.665
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

